{
  "_doc": "Headwaters source registry - Delhi episodic sources. Schema + design notes: docs/specs/headwaters.md (local). Delhi's live-feed story is unusual: its highest-cadence public source (DPCC monthly river + drain analysis) publishes as scanned PDFs on a Drupal listing, so edition detection here is what tells us a new month exists - the extraction itself is manual/OCR until that pipeline lands. MANUAL WATCH (not automatable here): the CGWB observation-well network behind public/data/delhi-cgwb-stations.json stopped reporting on 2025-09-20. Resumption would restore Delhi's only high-cadence groundwater signal, but it cannot be expressed as a registry check - the India-WRIS Ground Water Level endpoint needs a POST with mandatory query params, and while dormant it returns an empty array, so any api-date datePath would error rather than report no-change. Re-run neer-vazhvu-api/scripts/build_delhi_cgwb_stations.py --refresh to test.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "dpcc-monthly-analysis-delhi",
      "scope": "delhi",
      "publisher": "Delhi Pollution Control Committee",
      "url": "https://dpcc.delhi.gov.in/dpcc/analysis-reports",
      "license": "GNCTD publication, cited with attribution",
      "type": "pdf-listing",
      "cadence": "monthly",
      "tier": 1,
      "detection": {
        "method": "link-set",
        "linkPattern": "analysis-report/(river_yamuna|analysis_report_of_river|drain|analysis_report_of_drain|stp_analysis)"
      },
      "dependsOn": [
        "public/data/dpcc-monthly-wq-delhi.json",
        "public/data/river-quality-delhi.json"
      ],
      "refreshMethod": "manual (new month's river/drain/STP PDFs -> transcribe into dpcc-monthly-wq-delhi.json, then re-run scripts/build-delhi-river-quality.ts)",
      "notes": "THE Delhi feed: 8 Yamuna stations + ~39 drain points + STP compliance, sampled monthly and published around the 25th. A new file link = a new month. The drain 'NO FLOW' count in each edition is the verification instrument for the drain-trapping commitment. Feb-2026 is absent from the listing - confirm whether that is a publication gap when the next editions land.",
